-### U7. Craft & accessibility (folds into the most relevant dimension)
-- Contrast: body text ≥ WCAG AA 4.5:1 (`#aaa` on white ≈ 2.3:1 — fails; use ≥ `#595959`).
-- Click/tap targets ≥ 44×44px; body type ≥ 16px; visible focus states; responsive sanity (does a flex row wrap on mobile?).
+### U7. Craft & accessibility
+Assess this dimension explicitly; it may reference the same element as another dimension without counting the defect twice.
+- **Text contrast:** WCAG AA SC 1.4.3 uses 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text (18pt, or 14pt bold), subject to its exemptions. Obtain foreground/background colors and size/weight from reliable source or rendered styles; do not certify a ratio from appearance alone, round a failing ratio up, or prescribe one gray for every background.
+- **Pointer targets:** WCAG 2.2 AA SC 2.5.8 uses 24×24 **CSS pixels**, or one of its spacing/equivalent/inline/user-agent/essential exceptions. SC 2.5.5 is the stricter AAA 44×44 CSS-pixel criterion with its own exceptions; 44×44 is also a useful usability aim for important touch controls. A control below 44×44 is not automatically an AA failure. Inspect the actual hit area and applicable exception before judging.
+- **Text size:** 16px body text is a marketing-readability heuristic, not a WCAG AA minimum and not a universal rule for dense app screens. Judge legibility in context. SC 1.4.4 concerns text enlargement to 200% without loss of content/functionality, with its stated exceptions; test enlargement when an interactive page is available.
+- **Focus and responsive behavior:** inspect visible focus states, keyboard use and relevant viewport/zoom states when available. If only static evidence is supplied, mark those checks not assessed and name the follow-up needed. A single screenshot does not establish their behavior.
+
+Primary references (consulted 2026-10-15): [SC 1.4.3](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/contrast-minimum.html), [SC 1.4.4](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/resize-text.html), [SC 2.5.8](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/target-size-minimum.html), [SC 2.5.5](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/target-size-enhanced.html). These criteria inform this review; a full conformance assessment has a wider scope.
 
